ally reviewed and audited  their death figures sometimes  under directions from their respective  high courts  and therefore some of these corrections  have actually taken place it's not that  the absolute number of deaths  in the preceding week has been that high  uh and yes therefore  the debts that we have ended up with are  certainly higher than it seemed  and and some more states are going  through this correction or audit process  and the tally could actually be a little  higher than even what it seems now  well the health department in bihar one  of india's poorest states revised its  total covert related death toll from  some five and a half thousand two over  nine and a half  thousand on wednesday last week what's  going on is this  down to under reporting in some places  there is certainly an element of under  reporting  this is not necessarily to to indicate  that  that this has been deliberate but uh  it's part of the system coping up uh  there is  also uh the who advisory issued last  year as early as april 2020  as to what counts as a corporate death  and  uh it seems that the clarity of that  document of  of those definitions and and certainly  some of the  subtexts of those definitions uh perhaps  uh  didn't didn't really didn't really tell  you with what  what health departments were actually  doing and therefore as in the case of  bihar the high court of bihar  actually uh asked for this audit or  review process  and it's a and then this this this  change or the uptick in the figures is  really a culmination of that  what about this highly infectious delta  variant if i if i can butt in there  well the delta variant which is actually  the  sub lineage of v6171  was identified in india earlier this  year  in the southeastern districts of  the very last state of maharashtra it's  it's now subsequently  swept through through several large  states including delhi  delhi actually has been uh has been  affected both by the alpha variant as  well as by th